Requirements:
1. QEMU >= 8.2.10 because we use netduinoplus2 board.
   You may need to build from source because the QEMU installed with your Ubuntu may not be of the correct version.
   ref: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79610213/does-qemu-virt-board-really-support-cortex-m4-processor
2.


Preparation Steps:
0. Install toolchain
   sudo apt install ninja-build libglib2.0-dev flex bison

1. Build latest QEMU from source (ref: https://github.com/qemu/qemu)
   git clone git@github.com:qemu/qemu.git
   cd qemu
   mkdir build
   cd build
   ../configure
   make

2. Download ARM toolchain
   Goto: https://developer.arm.com/downloads/-/arm-gnu-toolchain-downloads
   wget https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu/14.3.rel1/binrel/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-eabi.tar.xz
   tar -vxf ./arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-eabi.tar.xz
   Change the toolchain path in the Makefile.


